2.2. Particle counts in consumables
The particle counts nMP of Senathirajah are taken from other studies that detected MP particles in the shellfish, salt, beer, and drinking water. The fact that the lower detection limit
amin
 affects the number of detected particles is not taken into account for the mi,MP calculation. The minimum particle size
amin
 of the cited studies is in the range of 5 μm, and detected particle counts nMP increase with decreasing
amin
, see Figure 2. For example, in the cited paper with the highest
amin
